===Proper HUD positioning for different aspect ratios===
{{ii}} For 16:10 change the value of <code>uiVerticalFrameScale</code> to <code>1.1253</code>.
{{ii}} For 21:9 change the value of <code>uiHorizontalFrameScale</code> to <code>1.3125</code>.

{{Fixbox|description=Edit user.settings config file|ref={{cn|date=July 2016}}|fix=
# Open {{file|{{p|userprofile\Documents}}\The Witcher 3\user.settings}} with a text editor.
# If your aspect ratio is vertically greater than 16:9 increase the value of <code>uiVerticalFrameScale</code> above 1.
# If your aspect ratio is horizontally greater than 16:9 increase the value of <code>uiHorizontalFrameScale</code> above 1.
}}

===Stutter while using a controller===
{{Fixbox|description=Edit the config file hidden.ini|ref={{cn|date=July 2016}}|fix=
# Open {{file|{{P|game}}\bin\config\base\hidden.ini}}.
# Change <code>LockControlScheme=0</code> to <code>LockControlScheme=2</code>.
# Save the file.

'''Notes'''
{{ii}} Stutter occurs because the game rapidly changes between controller and keyboard prompts.
{{ii}} This forces the game to use controller prompts.
{{ii}} There won't be any keyboard prompts even while using keyboard controls.
}}

===Increase shadow resolution distance===
{{ii}} Applies only to cascaded shadows. Ray Traced shadows are not affected.
{{Fixbox|description=Edit user.settings or dx12user.settings config file (depending on whether you run DirectX 11 or DirectX 12 version of the game)|fix=
# Set desired graphics settings before patching, since opening the settings after this patch will reset it.
# Set Shadow Quality to Ultra+
# Open {{file|{{p|userprofile\Documents}}\The Witcher 3\dx12user.settings}} with a text editor.
# Change the following values and save the file:
<code>CascadeShadowmapSize=8192</code><br>
<code>CascadeShadowDistanceScale0=8</code><br>
<code>CascadeShadowDistanceScale1=4</code><br>
<code>CascadeShadowDistanceScale2=2</code><br>
<code>CascadeShadowDistanceScale3=1</code>
}}

===FPS loss after VRAM 95% usage===

{{ii}} When Ray Tracing or Path Tracing is active, the game fails to clear cached asset data, causing VRAM to saturate. <br>This forces data into slow system RAM, which degrades performance.<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://forums.cdprojektred.com/index.php?threads/witcher-3-ng-ray-tracing-gpu-pci-e-bus-vram-overload-cause-of-fps-drop-stuttering-issue-fixed.11112562/page-3|title=Documentation of issue on CDPR Technical Forum|date=October 2026|s}}</ref><ref>{{Refurl|url=https://wccftech.com/the-witcher-3-next-gen-new-mod-fixes-ray-tracing-memory-leak-issues-increases-performance/|title=Detailed in performance analysis reviews on Wccftech.|date=October 2026}}</ref>

{{Fixbox|description=Lower specific VRAM-heavy graphical settings to keep utilization under 95%.|fix=
# Launch the game and go to '''Options''' > '''Video''' > '''Graphics'''.
# Set '''Texture Quality''' to '''High''' or '''Ultra''' instead of '''Ultra+'''.<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://forums.cdprojektred.com/index.php?threads/witcher-3-ng-ray-tracing-gpu-pci-e-bus-vram-overload-cause-of-fps-drop-stuttering-issue-fixed.11112562/page-3|title=Witcher 3 NG Ray Tracing - GPU PCI-E Bus / VRAM Overload cause of FPS drop/stuttering issue|publisher=CD PROJEKT RED Forums|date=2023-01-07}}</ref>
# Under the Ray Tracing section:
#* Keep '''Ray Tracing Global Illumination''' set to '''Performance''' (if enabled).
#* Disable '''Ray-Traced Reflections''' and '''Ray-Traced Shadows''', as each layer allocates significant additional VRAM buffers.
# Under '''Display''', set '''NVIDIA DLSS''' / upscaling to '''Quality''' or '''Balanced''' to decrease the internal render resolution and corresponding frame buffer size.
}}

{{Fixbox|description=NVIDIA: Set "CUDA - Sysmem Fallback Policy" to "Prefer No Sysmem Fallback" within NVIDIA Control Panel.|ref=<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250306190628/https://www.nexusmods.com/witcher3/mods/8083|title=Credit to user "vens162" in comment section |date=October 2026}}</ref>|fix=
# Open the NVIDIA Control Panel.
# Click on 	'''Manage 3D settings''' under the '''3D Settings''' list.
# Select the '''Program Settings''' tab.
# Select '''The Witcher 3''' (<code>witcher3.exe</code>) from the dropdown menu. <br>If it is not listed, click '''Add''' and locate the executable manually.
# Scroll down the list of settings to find '''CUDA - Sysmem Fallback Policy'''.
# Click the setting value and change it to '''Prefer No Sysmem Fallback'''.
# Click Apply in the bottom right corner to save your changes.
}}

